From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 19:29:27 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] soundwire: qcom: skip the clock stop handshake for the PMIC
 haptics port

The PMIC haptics SoundWire port, 0217:f002 (qcom,pm8550b-swr-haptics in
Qualcomm's downstream device tree), shares the WCD939x bus on SM8550 and
SM8650 boards and has no driver here. Without driver properties it is not
simple_clk_stop_capable, so clock stop prepare and de-prepare write its
SCP_SystemCtrl and wait for ClockStopNotFinished to clear. On the KONKR
Pocket FIT it keeps that bit set after de-prepare while the WCD9390
reports completion, so each s2idle resume waits out the clock stop
timeout and the speakers pop.

Add a peripheral quirk for devices that do not complete the clock stop
handshake, skip them in prepare and de-prepare, and set it for this
port when the Qualcomm controller enumerates it.
---
 drivers/soundwire/bus.c       |  6 ++++--
 drivers/soundwire/qcom.c      | 10 ++++++++++
 include/linux/soundwire/sdw.h |  2 ++
 3 files changed, 16 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/bus.c b/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
index a1e8f87a9..8548e4cf6 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/bus.c
@@ -1086,7 +1086,8 @@ int sdw_bus_prep_clk_stop(struct sdw_bus *bus)
 		}
 
 		/* Only prepare a Slave device if needed */
-		if (!slave->prop.simple_clk_stop_capable) {
+		if (!slave->prop.simple_clk_stop_capable &&
+		    !(slave->prop.quirks & SDW_SLAVE_QUIRKS_NO_CLK_STOP_PREP)) {
 			simple_clk_stop = false;
 
 			ret = sdw_slave_clk_stop_prepare(slave,
@@ -1209,7 +1210,8 @@ int sdw_bus_exit_clk_stop(struct sdw_bus *bus)
 			dev_warn(&slave->dev, "clock stop pre-deprepare cb failed:%d\n", ret);
 
 		/* Only de-prepare a Slave device if needed */
-		if (!slave->prop.simple_clk_stop_capable) {
+		if (!slave->prop.simple_clk_stop_capable &&
+		    !(slave->prop.quirks & SDW_SLAVE_QUIRKS_NO_CLK_STOP_PREP)) {
 			simple_clk_stop = false;
 
 			ret = sdw_slave_clk_stop_prepare(slave, SDW_CLK_STOP_MODE0,
diff --git a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
index 190fafc16..c993af852 100644
--- a/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
+++ b/drivers/soundwire/qcom.c
@@ -685,6 +685,16 @@ static int qcom_swrm_enumerate(struct sdw_bus *bus)
 		}
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The PMIC haptics port (qcom,pm8550b-swr-haptics downstream) has no
+	 * driver here and can keep ClockStopNotFinished set after de-prepare.
+	 */
+	mutex_lock(&bus->bus_lock);
+	list_for_each_entry(slave, &bus->slaves, node)
+		if (slave->id.mfg_id == 0x0217 && slave->id.part_id == 0xf002)
+			slave->prop.quirks |= SDW_SLAVE_QUIRKS_NO_CLK_STOP_PREP;
+	mutex_unlock(&bus->bus_lock);
+
 	complete(&ctrl->enumeration);
 	return 0;
 }
diff --git a/include/linux/soundwire/sdw.h b/include/linux/soundwire/sdw.h
index 79dd44922..87c207848 100644
--- a/include/linux/soundwire/sdw.h
+++ b/include/linux/soundwire/sdw.h
@@ -400,6 +400,8 @@ struct sdw_slave_prop {
 };
 
 #define SDW_SLAVE_QUIRKS_INVALID_INITIAL_PARITY	BIT(0)
+/* Skip SCP clock stop prepare and de-prepare accesses */
+#define SDW_SLAVE_QUIRKS_NO_CLK_STOP_PREP	BIT(1)
 
 /**
  * struct sdw_master_prop - Master properties
